@tradition late-piano
// Late piano (weekly, seat 15). The Captain plays the music-room piano on Tuesday and Thursday nights (the user's
// answer: two evenings; her musician habit already; 0.92.5, the user: "don't have them two nights in a row", so not
// Wednesday and Thursday any more); a few listen. Starts at 21:40, after the quiz; it's on Deck 4, so never on a deck
// with the evening's others. to-bed (0.92.5, the user: "no one actually comes, not even the captain"): it runs past
// most bedtimes, so whoever goes to bed in it still comes for 20 minutes or more and leaves 20 minutes before bed;
// and it starts at 21:40 (was 21:45), ten minutes after Tuesday's knit-and-natter and tiles and Thursday's quiz end (and a one-off show in the music room to 21:30 keeps its seats: section 14 holds a tradition's from 5 minutes before), so the Captain plays longer.
// Small and quiet on purpose. Design note: plans/trad-notes-weekly.md.
k: 438
title: Late piano
when: weekly tuesday,thursday
at: 21:40-22:25
min: 20
jitter: 10
to-bed: yes
where: 4 pool music
hold: 1
who: marrow always, music 55%, musician 40%, night-owl 25%, everyone 10%
anim: marrow play, everyone none
host: marrow
from: The music room
invite: host=marrow odds=10% line="I'll be at the piano later. Come and listen, if you like. I take requests. Sometimes."

== mail
- Late piano tomorrow, {time} in the music room, Deck 4. The Captain plays; anyone may listen. Quiet voices, please.

== ask
- The Captain's playing tonight, late. I'll be in the music room.
- Late piano tonight. I always mean to go to bed early. I never do.   #funny
- Going to hear the Captain play later. It's the calmest hour aboard.   #warm

== here
- Shh. This is the slow one.
- Listen to that. Who knew?   #warm
- I don't know what it's called. I just like it.

== thanks
- You slip into the music room and sit with the listeners. The Captain plays something slow and doesn't look up.   #warm

== chatter
- The Captain played something new the other night. Nobody asked what it was.   #warm
- I didn't know the Captain could play until my first week aboard.
- Late piano is the only time the Captain looks off duty.
